<header><p class="enc-kicker">Event · treaty</p><h1 class="enc-title">Treaty of Neuberg</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1379</span> · <a href="/centuries/14th-century">14th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Treaty of Neuberg was an agreement of 9 September 1379, signed at Neuberg Abbey in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/styria">Styria</a>, by which the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/habsburg-dynasty">Habsburg</a> brothers Albert III and Leopold III divided their lands. Albert kept the Duchy of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/austria">Austria</a> proper, founding the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/albertine-line">Albertine line</a>, while Leopold received Styria, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/carinthia">Carinthia</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/carniola">Carniola</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tyrol">Tyrol</a> and the western lands, founding the Leopoldine line. The Habsburg lands were reunited under Maximilian I in 1490.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/treaty-of-neuberg.jpg" alt="Treaty of Neuberg" width="320" height="407" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: User:Captain Blood · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:HRR_14Jh.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
